    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586-a1">

                <pb facs="0661" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg581"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bailey to Guatemalan minister of foreign affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June 6,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform your excellency
                    that I have received a note from the Department of State at Washington,
                    instructing me to advise the Government of your exellency that, while the
                    Government of the United States is indisposed to join in any collective act with
                    foreign powers which might have the aspect of coercive pressure upon the
                    Government of Guatemala respecting the payment of its foreign debt, it would
                    reserve for its citizens equal benefits with those which might be obtained for
                    creditors of any other nationality in the adjustment of said debt.</p>
                <p>I embrace the opportunity to renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Bailey.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
